# Text formatting: Preformatted keep and wrap, which keep spaces and line breaks, and Tab size.
Document (dev.stxt.pdf):
	Language: en
	Title: Text formatting · Preformatted text
	Page:
		Paper: A4
		Margin: 20mm
	Styles:
		For style: terminal
			Box:
				Margin: 0 0 16 0
				Padding: 8 10
				Background: sand
				Corner radius: 4
			Typography:
				Font: IBM Plex Mono
				Size: 9
				Line height: 13
	Section:
		Text: Text formatting
			Style: topic
		Heading 1:
			Text: Preformatted text
		Paragraph: With `Preformatted: keep`, the text keeps its spaces and line breaks, empty lines included, and a line wider than the box is an error. With `wrap`, a line that is too long breaks between words. `Tab size` is the width of a tab in characters.
			Style: intro
		Text: Preformatted: keep
			Style: label
		Text:
			Style: terminal
			Typography:
				Preformatted: keep
			Content >>
				$ thermostat --status
				temperature   21.5 °C
				setpoint      22.0 °C

				mode          heating
		Text: Preformatted: wrap  (in a box of 260 points)
			Style: label
		Text:
			Style: terminal
			Box:
				Width: 260
			Typography:
				Preformatted: wrap
			Content >>
				log: the connection to the server was closed after 30 seconds without an answer
				log: retrying in 5 seconds
		Text: Preformatted: none  (the default: the same lines become one paragraph)
			Style: label
		Text:
			Style: terminal
			Content >>
				$ thermostat --status
				temperature   21.5 °C
				setpoint      22.0 °C
		Text: Tab size: 4 and Tab size: 12, the same lines with tabs
			Style: label
		Text:
			Style: terminal
			Typography:
				Preformatted: keep
				Tab size: 4
			Content >>
				Item	Qty	Price
				Chair	12	145.00
				Table	1	890.00
		Text:
			Style: terminal
			Typography:
				Preformatted: keep
				Tab size: 12
			Content >>
				Item	Qty	Price
				Chair	12	145.00
				Table	1	890.00
